WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:09.400
Halloween is next week, meaning it's time
for a slew of virtue signaling articles and

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.740
think pieces on why every costume you want
to wear is racist, bigoted or some evil form

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.710
of cultural appropriation.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:21.320
Allow me to spare you the mental exhaustion
and propose something truly radical...wear

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:26.579
whatever the heck it is you want to wear this
Halloween.

00:00:26.579 --> 00:00:31.140
For me, it's gonna be the same Obi Wan Kenobi
costume I've worn for about the past 10 years,

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.770
though this year I think it'll look particularly
sharp with my new found beard.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:40.510
Forgetting the specifics of who's offended
by what today, the real issue here I'd like

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:46.360
to address is how the set of people who find
offense everywhere are actually doing something

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:50.899
much more offensive than any costume could
ever accomplish.

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:56.030
This endlessly outraged crowd are trying to
suck the joy out of every facet of life from

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.260
comedy to Halloween.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.560
It's just one of the many techniques these
control freaks masked as the good guys use

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:08.430
to whittle down your own sense of what's right
and wrong until you bow to their demand of

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.140
total conformity.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:15.270
Once they can get you to stop joking, stop
wearing costumes you want and most importantly

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:20.440
stop thinking for yourself, it's very easy
to manipulate you socially, politically or

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.440
otherwise.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.490
It's also one of the reasons we've seen so
many thoughtful, decent people purged by this

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.920
hysterical shrieking movement over the past
few years such as some of my former guests

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.600
like Bret Weinstein and Laura Kipnis.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:39.390
When conformity of thought is your number
one goal, then diversity of thought is your

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.890
number one enemy.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:45.280
This leaves little room for conversation,
comedy or costumes.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.160
It's precisely why comedy seems largely dead
right now.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:53.600
Who turns on late night TV to watch a comedian
lecture you about politics?

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.950
Come to think of it, who turns on latenight
comedy at all anymore?

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.130
What I wouldn't give for Johnny Carson to
be resurrected from the dead to show these

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:03.070
guys a thing or two.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:07.560
Actually, zombie Johnny Carson would be a
pretty great Halloween costume.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.269
Someone make it happen, I'll retweet you.

00:02:10.269 --> 00:02:14.800
Once conversation and honest debate is taken
away all that left is yelling.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.880
Once comedy is taken away all that's left
is lecturing and once costumes are taken away

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.390
all that's left is conformity.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:25.870
None of this adds up to how a healthy society
should operate.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.380
Does this mean that some conversations are
hard to have?

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.380
Yes.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.110
Does that mean that some jokes are offensive?

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.110
Indeed.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:35.250
Does it mean that some costumes might trigger
someone?

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.310
Absolutely.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:41.450
But we shouldn't trade in the distinctly human
trait of using our minds to talk, to joke,

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:46.750
or to express ourselves though dressing how
we please, just because it might offend someone.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:51.360
Of course with that all in mind, it's up to
you where that line from edginess to offense

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.360
is.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.260
This is what great satirists and comics and
writers have had to deal with for all time.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:01.051
If you get close to the line, you might just
trip over it, and rightly or wrongly, there

00:03:01.051 --> 00:03:04.310
probably will be consequences for your misstep.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:07.590
One year in high school I dressed up as an
Amish guy, one of my friends dressed up as

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.830
an Orthodox Jew and another dressed up as
a Catholic priest.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.560
We didn't do it to offend anyone, we did it
because it was different and in some ways

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.720
that's Halloween is all about.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:21.280
We also egged a bunch of houses and stole
candy, but fortunately that was before Twitter.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.420
As for me, I have no desire to go out of my
way to offend anyone, but I understand why

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:30.069
it's so important to live in a society that
allows us to do just that.

00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:34.940
So this Halloween whether you're a slutty
nun, a sexy pocahantas, or a good old fashioned

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:41.000
geisha, remember, it's better to be any of
those than a mindless, conformist zombie just

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:41.269
looking for brains.

